# Line endings, settled once.
#
# This repository had no `.gitattributes` and relied on `core.autocrlf`, which
# converts on checkout per machine. That meant the working tree could hold CRLF
# while the stored blobs held LF -- so any file git touched (a checkout, a
# stash pop, a restore) came back CRLF, and eslint, whose config enforces
# `linebreak-style: LF`, reported thousands of errors that were nothing to do
# with the code. It also broke text patterns anchored to "\n".
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` says it plainly: normalise text to LF in the repository and
# check it out as LF everywhere. Nothing in this project needs CRLF -- it is
# Node, Vue and GLSL, and the toolchain reads LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever the extension detector thinks.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.gdtf binary
*.mmfl binary
*.exe binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
